  {
    "episode_id": 84194,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84194.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 3,
    "turn_text": "One of the things that has been a priority for our task force is to get to the bottom of the planning and execution failures on the day of the Butler attack. So the state and local law enforcement officers were brought in to be part of the security operation that day and have really important insight for us about the planning, about the sites and how it was secured, about some of the breakdowns that happened that day. We know, for example, One of the critical failures related to communication between local law enforcement officers and the Secret Service agents who were there that day. So these witnesses are going to be able to walk us through the beginning to end of the planning and preparation for the day. And one of the purposes of this hearing, so we've been working really round the clocks since first. incident to get information, to do witnesses, to have brief things to review documents. But we want to also be sure we're sharing all of that with the American people. So this will be our first public hearing where the public gets to hear all of the same information that we are getting to hear. And that's a really critical thing to making sure that there's transparency and there's accountability.",
