  {
    "episode_id": 84194,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84194.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "So the second attack, and I'll start by saying, it was really shocking that we had a second attempt, and we had that so soon after the horrible events in Butler. We know that the Secret Service had been increasing the amount of security that was working with President Trump before the Palm Beach incident. So the fact that we had another attack or able to get this close is really just a shock. So on that second incident, we also will be requesting the same and reviewing and analyzing similar information. How did he get so close? What happened that day? We actually on that day, the agents who were right there with President Trump did a think goodness were able to identify and spot this would be attacker and make sure that that day wasn't any worse than it might have been. But the same type of information about what was the planning? What was the preparation? How was this person able to get so close? Do we need to have a broader security perimeter around President Trump at all times? And certainly, I believe we do. I think that his security detail needs to be elevated to a full presidential level security detail. The two things that are really important there are first, that he is a former president, but second, the reality of the threat environment. And we are seeing just an unprecedented threat environment right now in our country. So he needs every resource that can be provided to make sure that his future campaign stops and future activities are kept secure.",
