        "text": "At the time of the initial investigation, the suspect was facing firearm charges.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "An attempted assassination charge could result in a life sentence under federal law.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "There was concern that the federal government might not be able to bring sufficient charges against the suspect.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Federal prosecutors act based on available evidence and legal standards when deciding charges.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "A change in charges reflects improved understanding of the case by prosecutors.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Upgrading charges indicates stronger prosecutorial confidence in the strength of the case.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The public should view changes in criminal charges as meaningful indicators of investigative progress.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "Federal prosecution outcomes reflect institutional competence and integrity.",
